 {"id":"fabro-8296","title":"Make hidden-path glob return the fs_hide notice like grep does","status":"open","type":"task","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-09-07T20:12:20.817Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-07T20:22:11.003Z","description":"In the engine agent tool layer (`fabro-agent` glob tool), when a glob pattern targets paths hidden by fs_hide, return the same 'hidden from this stage by fs_hide' error grep produces instead of a silent empty result. This run's planner burned one LLM round plus 2 tool calls discovering the boundary: grep on `.fabro` errored correctly, but glob for `.fabro/workflows/**/*planner*` returned `is_error: false, output: \"\"` — indistinguishable from no-match. Optionally hoist the fs_hide rule in `.fabro/workflows/develop/prompts/planner.md` from step 3 to the tool-notes area. Effect: eliminates one wasted inference round per platform-path seed (the tracker's most common seed class). Not covered by open fabro-b7ab (docs) or fabro-8d61 (glob syntax docs).\nBasis: run 01M1YQD03JZJCGRJ53SNRBTM8P, workflow version 4ff76f32665f954e9a8e2027ec2a4a5b48266707730ae0620fcfd3f79acd4a10, commit 26c7ce34ffeb12df96dc464c485f83e5d1ba0b85","labels":["revision"],"assignee":"fabro"}
 {"id":"fabro-ab38","title":"Sweep open seeds against the merged run diff and mark satisfied siblings superseded","status":"open","type":"task","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-09-07T20:12:20.968Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-07T20:22:11.106Z","description":"Extend `.fabro/workflows/develop/scripts/closeout.nu` (or the improve workflow) with a post-merge sweep that greps the run's merged diff against open seeds targeting the same files and flags ones the change already satisfies. Evidence: this run's diff incidentally fixed the planner.md duplicate-'4.' numbering while open seed fabro-890d ('Renumber the duplicated step 4') stays open — nothing marks sibling seeds superseded, so the next planner can claim done work (the double-pick class fabro-d0c7 guarded only pre-merge). Distinct from fabro-aa46 (intake-time lint), fabro-fbed (closing the implemented seed itself), and fabro-c74f (journal clustering). Effect: tracker stays truthful after merges; prevents re-picking implemented work.\nBasis: run 01M1YQD03JZJCGRJ53SNRBTM8P, workflow version 4ff76f32665f954e9a8e2027ec2a4a5b48266707730ae0620fcfd3f79acd4a10, commit 26c7ce34ffeb12df96dc464c485f83e5d1ba0b85","labels":["revision"],"assignee":"fabro"}
 {"id":"fabro-6db3","title":"Classify the engine journal file as expected churn in evidence.nu","status":"open","type":"task","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-09-07T20:12:21.007Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-07T20:22:11.204Z","description":"In `.fabro/workflows/develop/scripts/evidence.nu`, add `.fabro/journal/**` (and `.fabro/blobs/**`) to the known-transient/churn section with an explicit '(engine journal, expected)' label. This run's reviewer found `.fabro/journal/<run>.jsonl +3` in its `git diff` beyond the churn list because the stage-journal hook writes after capture, and burned verification budget rationalizing an unexplained diff line instead of judging the seed. Distinct from open fabro-43ba (no-net-diff detection — the journal file grows monotonically) and fabro-93a7 (seed-spec paths). Effect: every review sees a reconciled churn list; removes a recurring false-deviation risk.\nBasis: run 01M1YQD03JZJCGRJ53SNRBTM8P, workflow version 4ff76f32665f954e9a8e2027ec2a4a5b48266707730ae0620fcfd3f79acd4a10, commit 26c7ce34ffeb12df96dc464c485f83e5d1ba0b85","labels":["revision"],"assignee":"fabro"}
-{"id":"fabro-05d0","title":"Bake gh into the develop toolchain image (or check open PRs engine-side) so the in-flight-PR guard functions","status":"open","type":"task","priority":1,"createdAt":"2026-09-07T20:40:40.695Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-07T20:56:07.508Z","description":"In run 01M1YS4NJH27NS7CQ02AWM9BNE the planner's mandated gh pr list --state open failed with exit 127 (gh: command not found) and degraded fail-open, so the double-pick guard from fabro-d0c7 (which exists because fabro-22e4 re-implemented a fix waiting in PR #47) is structurally disabled on fabro-toolchain:noble even though the engine has GitHub access (PR #51 was created). Change: add the gh binary to the toolchain image built from .fabro/Dockerfile, or move the open-PR check engine-side using run PR metadata instead of a sandbox binary. Expected effect: the guard actually audits double-picks and one guaranteed erroring tool call disappears from every planning pass.\nBasis: run 01M1YS4NJH27NS7CQ02AWM9BNE, workflow version ae2869aca84cea61832e77a2926b97ebb79d70300014555c724f2862e12612c9, commit 774f67e9548357656f837bd152c22be72920eb1e","labels":["revision"],"assignee":"fabro"}
+{"id":"fabro-05d0","title":"Bake gh into the develop toolchain image (or check open PRs engine-side) so the in-flight-PR guard functions","status":"in_progress","type":"task","priority":1,"createdAt":"2026-09-07T20:40:40.695Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-07T21:02:55.056Z","description":"In run 01M1YS4NJH27NS7CQ02AWM9BNE the planner's mandated gh pr list --state open failed with exit 127 (gh: command not found) and degraded fail-open, so the double-pick guard from fabro-d0c7 (which exists because fabro-22e4 re-implemented a fix waiting in PR #47) is structurally disabled on fabro-toolchain:noble even though the engine has GitHub access (PR #51 was created). Change: add the gh binary to the toolchain image built from .fabro/Dockerfile, or move the open-PR check engine-side using run PR metadata instead of a sandbox binary. Expected effect: the guard actually audits double-picks and one guaranteed erroring tool call disappears from every planning pass.\nBasis: run 01M1YS4NJH27NS7CQ02AWM9BNE, workflow version ae2869aca84cea61832e77a2926b97ebb79d70300014555c724f2862e12612c9, commit 774f67e9548357656f837bd152c22be72920eb1e","labels":["revision"],"assignee":"fabro"}
 {"id":"fabro-5b0a","title":"Surface degraded fail-open planner checks as run-level warnings in the run summary and PR body","status":"open","type":"task","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-09-07T20:40:43.171Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-07T20:56:07.608Z","description":"In run 01M1YS4NJH27NS7CQ02AWM9BNE the gh open-PR check degraded fail-open but the degradation was visible only in a journal line; a human reading PR #51 cannot distinguish 'succeeded' from 'succeeded with guards down'. Change: engine-side, emit a run-level warning (surfaced in the run summary and the PR body) whenever a mandated planner check degrades fail-open instead of logging it only to the journal. Expected effect: guard-down runs become human-visible at review time instead of silently passing.\nBasis: run 01M1YS4NJH27NS7CQ02AWM9BNE, workflow version ae2869aca84cea61832e77a2926b97ebb79d70300014555c724f2862e12612c9, commit 774f67e9548357656f837bd152c22be72920eb1e","labels":["revision"],"assignee":"fabro"}
